[{"ID":1,"Title":"Intro","Text":"<span style=\"font-size:24pt\">A new kind of variable is now available in 4D: <span style=\"font-style:italic;font-weight:bold\">Collection</span>.<br/>They can be declared with a new declaration command:<br/><span style=\"color:#0051BA\"><br/><span style=\"font-weight:bold\">C_COLLECTION</span>(myCollection)<br/></span><br/><br/>Collections can be filled with the command \"New collection\" and they can contain almost any kind of data like strings, numbers, dates, booleans, objects as well as other collections.<br/><br/><span style=\"color:#0051BA\"><span style=\"color:#BF30B5\">col1</span>:= <span style=\"font-weight:bold\">New collection</span>(12;\"alpha\";\"zoulou\";45)<br/><span style=\"color:#009E60\">col2</span>:= <span style=\"font-weight:bold\">New collection</span>(50;\"bravo\";<span style=\"color:#BF30B5\">col1</span>;<span style=\"font-family:'Menlo';font-weight:bold\">Current date</span>)<br/><span style=\"color:#CC7A02\">col3</span>:= <span style=\"font-weight:bold\">New collection</span>(<span style=\"color:#BF30B5\">col1</span>;<span style=\"color:#009E60\">col2</span>)<br/></span></span>","SampleSort":10},{"ID":2,"Title":"Stringify","Text":"<span style=\"font-weight:bold\"><span style=\"font-size:24pt;font-weight:normal\">Collections can be <span style=\"font-style:italic;font-weight:bold\">stringified</span> just like object type variables.<br/></span><br/><br/><span style=\"font-size:18pt;color:#0051BA;font-weight:normal\"><span style=\"color:#BF30B5\">col1</span>:= <span style=\"font-weight:bold\">New collection</span>(12;\"alpha\";\"zoulou\";45)<br/><span style=\"color:#009E60\">col2</span>:= <span style=\"font-weight:bold\">New collection</span>(50;\"bravo\";<span style=\"color:#BF30B5\">col1</span>;<span style=\"font-family:'Menlo';font-weight:bold\">True</span>)<br/><span style=\"color:#CC7A02\">col3</span>:= <span style=\"font-weight:bold\">New collection</span>(<span style=\"color:#BF30B5\">col1</span>;<span style=\"color:#009E60\">col2</span>)<br/><br/><span style=\"font-family:'Menlo';font-size:14pt;color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:18pt\"><span style=\"color:#0432FF\">vString</span>:=<span style=\"color:#2B8942;font-weight:bold\">JSON Stringify</span>(<span style=\"font-family:'Lucida Grande';color:#BF30B5\">col1</span>;*)<br/><span style=\"color:#0432FF\">vString</span>:=<span style=\"color:#2B8942;font-weight:bold\">JSON Stringify</span>(<span style=\"font-family:'Lucida Grande';color:#009E60\">col2</span>;*)<br/><span style=\"color:#0432FF\">vString</span>:=<span style=\"color:#2B8942;font-weight:bold\">JSON Stringify</span>(<span style=\"font-family:'Lucida Grande';color:#CC7A02\">col3</span>;*)</span><br/></span><br/><br/><br/><br/><br/><br/><span style=\"font-size:24pt;color:#000000\">Strings can also be <span style=\"font-style:italic;font-weight:bold\">parsed</span> to be turned into collections.<br/><br/><span style=\"font-family:'Menlo';font-size:18pt\"><span style=\"color:#877530\">col</span>:=<span style=\"color:#2B8942;font-weight:bold\">JSON Parse</span>(<span style=\"color:#0432FF\">vString2</span>)</span></span></span></span>","SampleSort":20},{"ID":9,"Title":"Object notation (0)","Text":"<span style=\"font-size:24pt\"><span style=\"font-weight:bold\">Important note</span>:<br/><br/>In order to be able to access each item of collections in your databases, make sure you activated the <span style=\"color:#0051BA;font-weight:bold\">object notation</span> in the Compatibility panel of the Database settings.<br/><br/>See on <span style=\"font-weight:bold\">next page</span> what this notation allows to do!</span>","SampleSort":30},{"ID":10,"Title":"Object notation (1)","Text":"<span style=\"font-size:24pt\">Collections are <span style=\"color:#0051BA;font-weight:bold\">variables</span>, <span style=\"color:#EF6B00;font-weight:bold\">not arrays</span>. That is the reason why their content can <span style=\"color:#EF6B00;font-weight:bold\">not</span> be accessed using curved brakets <span style=\"color:#EF6B00;font-weight:bold\">{}</span> but <span style=\"font-weight:bold\">square</span> brakets <span style=\"color:#0051BA;font-weight:bold\">[ ]</span> !<br/><br/>Also not that the <span style=\"color:#EF6B00;font-weight:bold\">first</span> item of collection is numbered <span style=\"color:#EF6B00;font-weight:bold\">zero</span>!<br/><br/><span style=\"font-family:'Menlo';font-size:14pt\"><span style=\"font-size:24pt\"><span style=\"color:#AA753F\">$obj</span>:=<span style=\"color:#2B8942;font-weight:bold\">OB New</span>(\"val\";\"Echo\")<br/></span><br/></span><span style=\"color:#BF30B5\">col</span>:= <span style=\"color:#0051BA;font-weight:bold\">New collection</span>(12;\"alpha\";<span style=\"color:#AA753F\">$</span><span style=\"font-family:'Menlo'\"><span style=\"color:#AA753F\">obj</span>;<span style=\"color:#2B8942;font-weight:bold\">True</span></span>)<br/><br/>vNum:=<span style=\"color:#BF30B5\">col</span><span style=\"color:#0051BA;font-weight:bold\">[<span style=\"color:#EF6B00\">0</span>]</span><br/>vString:=<span style=\"color:#BF30B5\">col</span><span style=\"color:#0051BA;font-weight:bold\">[<span style=\"color:#000000\">1</span>]</span><br/>obj:=<span style=\"color:#BF30B5\">col</span><span style=\"color:#0051BA;font-weight:bold\">[<span style=\"color:#000000\">2</span>]</span><br/>boo:=<span style=\"color:#BF30B5\">col</span><span style=\"color:#0051BA;font-weight:bold\">[<span style=\"color:#000000\">3</span>]</span></span>","SampleSort":40},{"ID":12,"Title":"OB SET/Get","Text":"<span style=\"font-size:24pt\">Collections can be set into objets and get from objects.<br/>Simply use <span style=\"color:#0051BA;font-weight:bold\">OB SET</span> and <span style=\"color:#0051BA;font-weight:bold\">OB Get</span> functions.<br/><br/><span style=\"font-size:18pt;color:#0051BA\"><span style=\"color:#BF30B5\">col1</span>:= <span style=\"font-weight:bold\">New collection</span>(10;12;18;24)<br/><span style=\"color:#009E60\">col2</span>:= <span style=\"font-weight:bold\">New collection</span>(\"Arial\";\"Times\";\"Verdana\")<br/><br/><span style=\"font-weight:bold\">OB SET</span>(<span style=\"color:#000000\">obj;\"sizes\";</span><span style=\"color:#BF30B5\">col1</span>)<br/><span style=\"font-weight:bold\">OB SET</span>(<span style=\"color:#000000\">obj;\"fonts\";</span><span style=\"color:#009E60\">col2</span>)<br/><br/><br/>-----<br/><br/><br/><span style=\"font-weight:bold\"><span style=\"color:#BF30B5;font-weight:normal\">col1:=</span>OB Get</span>(<span style=\"color:#000000\">obj;\"sizes\"</span>)<br/><span style=\"font-weight:bold\"><span style=\"color:#009E60;font-weight:normal\">col2:=</span>OB Get</span>(<span style=\"color:#000000\">obj;\"fonts\"</span>)<br/></span></span>","SampleSort":25},{"ID":13,"Title":"Object notation (2)","Text":"<span style=\"font-family:'Menlo';font-size:24pt\"><span style=\"font-family:'Lucida Grande'\">Collections do <span style=\"font-weight:bold\">not</span> need to be sized when initialized.<br/>The code below is valid!<br/></span><br/><span style=\"color:#2B8942;font-weight:bold\"><br/></span><span style=\"color:#0432FF\">col</span>:=<span style=\"color:#2B8942;font-weight:bold\">New collection<br/><br/></span><span style=\"color:#0432FF\">col</span>[<span style=\"color:#BF30B5;font-weight:bold\">0</span>]:=\"Alpha\"<br/><span style=\"color:#0432FF\">col</span>[<span style=\"color:#BF30B5;font-weight:bold\">5</span>]:=\"Foxtrot\"<br/><span style=\"color:#0432FF\">col</span>[<span style=\"color:#BF30B5;font-weight:bold\">10</span>]:=\"Lima\"</span>","SampleSort":50},{"ID":14,"Title":"Properties","Text":"<span style=\"font-family:'Menlo';font-size:18pt\"><span style=\"color:#0432FF\"><span style=\"font-size:24pt;color:#000000\">You can use the object notation to get properties.</span><br/><br/>col</span>:=<span style=\"color:#2B8942;font-weight:bold\">New collection<br/></span><span style=\"color:#0432FF\">col</span>[0]:=\"Alpha\"<br/><span style=\"color:#0432FF\">col</span>[2]:=<span style=\"color:#2B8942;font-weight:bold\">False<br/></span><span style=\"color:#0432FF\">col</span>[4]:=\"Bravo\"<br/><span style=\"color:#0432FF\">col</span>[6]:=48.6<br/><span style=\"color:#0432FF\">col</span>[10]:=<span style=\"color:#2B8942;font-weight:bold\">OB New</span>(\"a\";\"alpha\")<br/><span style=\"color:#0432FF\">col</span>[13]:=<span style=\"color:#2B8942;font-weight:bold\">True<br/></span><span style=\"color:#0432FF\">col</span>[17]:=999<br/><span style=\"color:#0432FF\">col</span>[23]:=<span style=\"color:#2B8942;font-weight:bold\">OB New</span>(\"z\";\"zoulou\")<br/><br/><span style=\"color:#AA753F;font-weight:bold\">// This is the way to know the number of items of a collection!<br/>// <span style=\"color:#D81E05\">length</span> is a property of collection!<br/><br/></span><span style=\"color:#AA753F\">$n</span>:=<span style=\"color:#0432FF\">col</span><span style=\"color:#B0927E\"><span style=\"color:#AA753F\"><span style=\"color:#D81E05;font-weight:bold\">.length</span>  </span><br/></span><span style=\"color:#0051BA\">vString</span>:=\"The collection contains \"+<span style=\"color:#2B8942;font-weight:bold\">String</span>(<span style=\"color:#946933\">$n</span>-1)+\" items! \"<br/><br/><span style=\"font-weight:bold\">For</span>($i;<span style=\"font-weight:bold\"><span style=\"color:#D81E05\">0</span>;<span style=\"color:#D81E05\">$n-1</span></span>)<br/>   … (see code inside the button!)…<br/><span style=\"font-weight:bold\">End for</span></span>","SampleSort":60}]